{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:d6172699a45fea54","name":"The Mecrosa Order","source":{"id":"source:reference-d6172699a45fea54","title":"The Mecrosa Order","revision":24104,"timestamp":"2024-10-20T15:54:21Z","sha256":"c6696b7db9ec265d65b9043df4d720082bb098a42f119d4f1d67f5501740419b","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=24104","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=The%20Mecrosa%20Order&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-d6172699a45fea54","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["For centuries, a secret evil in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Tapani Sector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Tapani_Sector?action=edit&redlink=1"}," has had nobles and commoners jumping at shadows in their own homes and palaces. That evil is The Mecrosa Order, and its nefarious leader is ",{"tag":"a","children":["High Lady Brezwalt III"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/High_Lady_Brezwalt_III"},". Descendants from an ancient order of Sith settled in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Tapani Sector"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Tapani_Sector?action=edit&redlink=1"},", and years later a young noblewoman would rediscover her ancient Sith heritage. She founds The Mecrosa Order: a coalition of Force-sensitive knights sworn to protect Mecetti's High Lord and Lady. These Sith Lords are granted tax-free holdings on the world ",{"tag":"a","children":["Nyssa"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Nyssa?action=edit&redlink=1"},"; over two centuries, Mecrosa grows immensely wealthy and powerful, developing chapter houses, palazzi, and spynets throughout the sector.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Yet, the aloof Tapanis value their independence from the Republic above all. Despite ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi","referenceId":"reference:d320edb17de6c558"}," ties of Mecetti's archnemesis ",{"tag":"a","children":["House Pelagia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Pelagia","referenceId":"reference:ab25390ffed4576f"},", Tapanis refuse outlander meddling in this \"minor domestic affair.\" So when ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Sith War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Sith_War"}," erupts, the young cutthroat Mecrosa matron ",{"tag":"a","children":["High Lady Brezwalt III"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/High_Lady_Brezwalt_III"},", part of a dynasty of Mecetti rulers of ",{"tag":"a","children":["Tapani Nobility"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Tapani_Nobility","referenceId":"reference:116393e4f9b4af65"},", brazenly endeavors to seize control of half the sector. During Tapani Day festivities, her ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Assassins"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Assassins"}," attempt simultaneous assassinations of five of the eight rival house leaders, including Reena, Pelagia, Melissus, Calipsa, and Barong. Of these, only Pelagia foils the plot, while Houses Calipsa, Melissus, Barong, and a clump of Reena are absorbed into Mecetti Province. The Mecrosa Order, long a mere myth, now brutally showcases its reality.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["At last, ",{"tag":"a","children":["House Pelagia"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Pelagia","referenceId":"reference:ab25390ffed4576f"}," and ",{"tag":"a","children":["House Melantha"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Melantha","referenceId":"reference:8ff9885b927aacde"}," beg for Republic intervention, but with Exar Kun's war intensifying, no help comes. ",{"tag":"a","children":["High Lady Brezwalt III"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/High_Lady_Brezwalt_III"}," stands poised to transform Tapani Sector into the Mecetti Empire, until Pelagian ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Shadows"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Shadows"}," turn the tables. Infiltrating every Mecrosa chapter, the Jedi double agents wait. Then, when ",{"tag":"a","children":["Exar Kun"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Exar_Kun","referenceId":"reference:ecc01bec6de14936"}," is defeated, the Shadows spring their trap and ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Jedi Order"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Jedi_Order"}," pounces. In this event, known as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Cleansing of the Nine Houses"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Cleansing_of_the_Nine_Houses?action=edit&redlink=1"},", Jedi Knights destroy The Mecrosa Order, and Mecetti nobles, anxious to save face, turn against Lady Brezwalt.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Mecrosa Order Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Nonheroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Assassin"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Assassin","referenceId":"reference:80109ea9b882a4d2"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 6\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Bladeborn"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Bladeborn","referenceId":"reference:3319efb714f07542"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 10\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Heroic Units"]},"\n",{"tag":"table","children":["\n",{"tag":"tbody","children":[{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"th","children":["NAME\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["CHALLENGE LEVEL\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"th","children":["SOURCE\n"]}]},"\n",{"tag":"tr","children":["\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Brezwalt III"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Brezwalt_III","referenceId":"reference:13c2c69aa66deed3"},"\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":["CL 16\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"td","children":[{"tag":"i","children":[{"tag":"a","children":["Knights of the Old Republic Campaign Guide"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Knights_of_the_Old_Republic_Campaign_Guide"}]},"\n"]}]}]}]},"\n","\n",{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"br","children":[]},"\n"]},"\n","\n","\n","\n\n","\n\n","\n"]}}
